    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, my electric water heater is making this really loud knocking sound every now and then and the water isnt staying hot anymore. any idea what it could be or do i just need to call a plumber?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Loud knocking sounds and a loss of heat in your electric water heater could be caused by sediment buildup or an evaporator coil issue. Start by turning off the heater, evacuate the tank, and clear out any sediment. Check the evaporator coil in the attic; if it's covered in frost, the water might not be evaporating and therefore not heating properly. If you've tried these steps and still have issues, calling a plumber may be wise to avoid potential water damage or electrical hazards.",
      "source": "target",
